    "{\n",
    " \"cells\": [\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Data Analytics Assignment — Question 3\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Measuring Data Similarity & Dissimilarity\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Datasets:** wine.csv + nutrient.csv\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## Part A – Data Matrix vs. Dissimilarity Matrix on Wine Data (6 Marks)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Import required libraries\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import pandas as pd\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import numpy as np\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import seaborn as sns\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from scipy.spatial.distance import cdist\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Set display options\\n\",\n",
    "    \"pd.set_option('display.max_columns', None)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"pd.set_option('display.width', None)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"pd.set_option('display.precision', 2)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Set plot style\\n\",\n",
    "    \"sns.set_style('whitegrid')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.rcParams['figure.figsize'] = (10, 8)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('Libraries imported successfully!')\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Task 18: Load wine.csv and select first 10 rows with 6 numeric attributes\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Load the wine dataset\\n\",\n",
    "    \"url_wine = \\\"https://drive.google.com/uc?export=download&id=1_2u0kE9Q5W4m3S7R8-X0N1o2p3L4K5J6\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"wine_df = pd.read_csv(url_wine)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Select the six numeric attributes\\n\",\n",
    "    \"selected_columns = ['Alcohol', 'Malic', 'Ash', 'Magnesium', 'Phenols', 'Flavanoids']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Select first 10 rows\\n\",\n",
    "    \"wine_subset = wine_df[selected_columns].head(10)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('=== Wine Dataset - First 10 Rows, 6 Numeric Attributes ===')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'Shape: {wine_subset.shape}')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(wine_subset)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Task 19 – 10 × 6 Data Matrix (Formatted DataFrame)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Task 19: Display the 10 × 6 data matrix as a formatted DataFrame\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Reset index to show row numbers starting from 1\\n\",\n",
    "    \"data_matrix = wine_subset.copy()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"data_matrix.index = range(1, 11)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('=== 10 × 6 Data Matrix ===')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('Rows = Wine Samples (Observations)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('Columns = Chemical Attributes (Attributes)')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(data_matrix.round(2))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('\\\\n=== Data Matrix Statistics ===')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'Number of observations: {data_matrix.shape[0]}')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'Number of attributes: {data_matrix.shape[1]}')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'Total data points: {data_matrix.shape[0] * data_matrix.shape[1]}')\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Task 20 – Euclidean Dissimilarity Matrix\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Task 20: Compute and display 10 × 10 Euclidean dissimilarity matrix\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Compute Euclidean distance matrix using cdist\\n\",\n",
    "    \"euclidean_dist = cdist(wine_subset.values, wine_subset.values, metric='euclidean')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Create DataFrame with proper labels\\n\",\n",
    "    \"euclidean_df = pd.DataFrame(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    euclidean_dist,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    index=[f'Wine {i}' for i in range(1, 11)],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    columns=[f'Wine {i}' for i in range(1, 11)]\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('=== Euclidean Dissimilarity Matrix (10 × 10) ===')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(euclidean_df.round(3))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Visualize as heatmap\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.figure(figsize=(10, 8))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"sns.heatmap(euclidean_df, annot=True, fmt='.2f', cmap='YlOrRd', \\n\",\n",
    "    \"            cbar_kws={'label': 'Euclidean Distance'}, square=True,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            linewidths=0.5, linecolor='white')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.title('Euclidean Dissimilarity Matrix - Wine Samples', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.xlabel('Wine Samples', fontsize=12)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.ylabel('Wine Samples', fontsize=12)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('\\\\n=== Euclidean Distance Statistics ===')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Get upper triangle values (excluding diagonal)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"upper_tri_euclidean = euclidean_dist[np.triu_indices_from(euclidean_dist, k=1)]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'Min distance (excluding self): {upper_tri_euclidean.min():.3f}')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'Max distance: {upper_tri_euclidean.max():.3f}')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'Mean distance: {upper_tri_euclidean.mean():.3f}')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'Std distance: {upper_tri_euclidean.std():.3f}')\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Task 21 – Manhattan Dissimilarity Matrix\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Task 21: Compute and display 10 × 10 Manhattan (L1) dissimilarity matrix\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Compute Manhattan distance matrix using cdist\\n\",\n",
    "    \"manhattan_dist = cdist(wine_subset.values, wine_subset.values, metric='cityblock')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Create DataFrame with proper labels\\n\",\n",
    "    \"manhattan_df = pd.DataFrame(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    manhattan_dist,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    index=[f'Wine {i}' for i in range(1, 11)],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    columns=[f'Wine {i}' for i in range(1, 11)]\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('=== Manhattan (L1) Dissimilarity Matrix (10 × 10) ===')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(manhattan_df.round(3))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Visualize as heatmap\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.figure(figsize=(10, 8))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"sns.heatmap(manhattan_df, annot=True, fmt='.2f', cmap='YlOrRd', \\n\",\n",
    "    \"            cbar_kws={'label': 'Manhattan Distance'}, square=True,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            linewidths=0.5, linecolor='white')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.title('Manhattan (L1) Dissimilarity Matrix - Wine Samples', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.xlabel('Wine Samples', fontsize=12)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.ylabel('Wine Samples', fontsize=12)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('\\\\n=== Manhattan Distance Statistics ===')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"upper_tri_manhattan = manhattan_dist[np.triu_indices_from(manhattan_dist, k=1)]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'Min distance (excluding self): {upper_tri_manhattan.min():.3f}')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'Max distance: {upper_tri_manhattan.max():.3f}')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'Mean distance: {upper_tri_manhattan.mean():.3f}')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'Std distance: {upper_tri_manhattan.std():.3f}')\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Comparison: Euclidean vs. Manhattan Distance\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Side-by-side comparison of both distance matrices\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(20, 8))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Euclidean heatmap\\n\",\n",
    "    \"sns.heatmap(euclidean_df, annot=True, fmt='.2f', cmap='YlOrRd', \\n\",\n",
    "    \"            cbar_kws={'label': 'Euclidean Distance'}, square=True,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            linewidths=0.5, linecolor='white', ax=axes[0])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"axes[0].set_title('Euclidean Distance (L2)', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"axes[0].set_xlabel('Wine Samples')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"axes[0].set_ylabel('Wine Samples')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Manhattan heatmap\\n\",\n",
    "    \"sns.heatmap(manhattan_df, annot=True, fmt='.2f', cmap='YlOrRd', \\n\",\n",
    "    \"            cbar_kws={'label': 'Manhattan Distance'}, square=True,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            linewidths=0.5, linecolor='white', ax=axes[1])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"axes[1].set_title('Manhattan Distance (L1)', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"axes[1].set_xlabel('Wine Samples')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"axes[1].set_ylabel('Wine Samples')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('\\\\n=== Comparison Analysis ===')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'Euclidean - Mean: {upper_tri_euclidean.mean():.3f}, Max: {upper_tri_euclidean.max():.3f}')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'Manhattan - Mean: {upper_tri_manhattan.mean():.3f}, Max: {upper_tri_manhattan.max():.3f}')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'\\\\nManhattan distances are consistently LARGER than Euclidean distances.')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'Ratio (Manhattan/Euclidean) mean: {upper_tri_manhattan.mean() / upper_tri_euclidean.mean():.3f}')\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"**Which distance metric produces more extreme dissimilarity values? Why?**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Answer:** The **Manhattan (L1) distance** produces more extreme (larger) dissimilarity values compared to Euclidean (L2) distance. This is evident from the statistics above where Manhattan distances are consistently larger.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Why?** \\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Euclidean distance** calculates the straight-line (shortest) distance between two points: $d = \\\\sqrt{\\\\sum (x_i - y_i)^2}$\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Manhattan distance** sums the absolute differences along each dimension: $d = \\\\sum |x_i - y_i|$\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Manhattan distance tends to be larger because it accumulates differences across all dimensions without the squaring-square root operation that moderates Euclidean distance. In high-dimensional spaces, Manhattan distance gives equal weight to all attribute differences, making it more sensitive to differences spread across multiple attributes, while Euclidean distance is more influenced by large differences in fewer attributes due to the squaring operation.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Part B – Minkowski Distance Experiment (5 Marks)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Task 22: Choose three wine samples and compute pairwise Minkowski distance\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Select three wine samples (rows 1, 5, and 9 - using 0-based indexing: 0, 4, 8)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"wine_1 = wine_subset.iloc[0].values  # Wine sample 1\\n\",\n",
    "    \"wine_2 = wine_subset.iloc[4].values  # Wine sample 5\\n\",\n",
    "    \"wine_3 = wine_subset.iloc[8].values  # Wine sample 9\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('=== Selected Wine Samples ===')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'Wine Sample 1: {wine_subset.iloc[0].values}')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'Wine Sample 5: {wine_subset.iloc[4].values}')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'Wine Sample 9: {wine_subset.iloc[8].values}')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Define Minkowski distance function\\n\",\n",
    "    \"def minkowski_distance(x, y, p):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Compute Minkowski distance between two vectors for parameter p.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Parameters:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    x, y: numpy arrays or lists\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    p: Minkowski parameter (p >= 1)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Returns:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Minkowski distance value\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return np.power(np.sum(np.abs(x - y) ** p), 1/p)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Define p values to test\\n\",\n",
    "    \"p_values = [1, 2, 3, 10]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Create pairs\\n\",\n",
    "    \"pairs = [\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ('Wine 1 vs Wine 5', wine_1, wine_2),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ('Wine 1 vs Wine 9', wine_1, wine_3),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ('Wine 5 vs Wine 9', wine_2, wine_3)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Compute Minkowski distances for all pairs and p values\\n\",\n",
    "    \"results = {}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for pair_name, x, y in pairs:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    results[pair_name] = []\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for p in p_values:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        dist = minkowski_distance(x, y, p)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        results[pair_name].append(dist)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Create results DataFrame\\n\",\n",
    "    \"results_df = pd.DataFrame(results, index=[f'p={p}' for p in p_values])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('\\\\n=== Minkowski Distance Table ===')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(results_df.round(4))\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Task 23: Plot line chart of Minkowski distances\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Plot each pair\\n\",\n",
    "    \"colors = ['blue', 'red', 'green']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"markers = ['o', 's', '^']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for idx, (pair_name, x, y) in enumerate(pairs):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    distances = [minkowski_distance(x, y, p) for p in p_values]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    plt.plot(p_values, distances, marker=markers[idx], linewidth=2, \\n\",\n",
    "    \"             markersize=8, label=pair_name, color=colors[idx])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.xlabel('Minkowski Parameter (p)', fontsize=12)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.ylabel('Minkowski Distance', fontsize=12)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.title('Minkowski Distance vs. Parameter p', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.legend(fontsize=10)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.xticks(p_values)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('\\\\n=== Minkowski Distance Trends ===')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for pair_name, x, y in pairs:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    dist_p1 = minkowski_distance(x, y, 1)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    dist_p10 = minkowski_distance(x, y, 10)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f'{pair_name}: p=1 → {dist_p1:.4f}, p=10 → {dist_p10:.4f}')\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Task 24 – Effect of Increasing p on Distance Value\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"**Explanation: Effect of Increasing p on Minkowski Distance**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"As the parameter **p increases**, the Minkowski distance exhibits the following behavior:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. **p = 1**: Manhattan distance - sums all absolute differences equally\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. **p = 2**: Euclidean distance - the standard straight-line distance\\n\",\n",
    "    \"3. **p = 3, 10, ...**: As p increases, the distance becomes increasingly dominated by the **largest single difference** between any one attribute\\n\",\n",
    "    \"4. **p → ∞**: Approaches **Chebyshev distance** (L∞ norm)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Mathematical Explanation:**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The Minkowski distance formula is:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"$$d_p(x, y) = \\\\left(\\\\sum_{i=1}^{n} |x_i - y_i|^p\\\\right)^{1/p}$$\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"As **p → ∞**, the term with the **largest absolute difference** dominates the sum because raising to a large power amplifies larger values much more than smaller ones. Mathematically:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"$$\\\\lim_{p \\\\to \\\\infty} d_p(x, y) = \\\\max_i(|x_i - y_i|)$$\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"This is the **Chebyshev distance** (also called L∞ norm or maximum metric).\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Key Observations from the Plot:**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Distance values **increase** as p increases (but at a decreasing rate)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- The curve **flattens** as p gets larger, approaching an asymptote\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- This asymptote equals the **maximum absolute difference** across all attributes (Chebyshev distance)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- The effect is consistent across all wine sample pairs\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Practical Implication:** \\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Low p values (p=1, 2) consider **all attribute differences**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- High p values focus on the **single largest difference**, ignoring smaller differences\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Chebyshev distance is useful when the worst-case difference matters most\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Part C – Proximity for Nominal & Binary Attributes on Nutrient Data (5 Marks)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Load nutrient dataset\\n\",\n",
    "    \"url_nutrient = \\\"https://drive.google.com/uc?export=download&id=1_3v1lF0R6X5n4T8S9-Y1O2p3q4M5N6O7\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"nutrient_df = pd.read_csv(url_nutrient)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('=== Nutrient Dataset ===')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(nutrient_df)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'\\\\nShape: {nutrient_df.shape}')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'\\\\nColumns: {list(nutrient_df.columns)}')\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Task 25 – Proximity for Nominal Attributes\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Task 25: Compute similarity based on energy and fat groups (Low/Medium/High)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Step 1: Categorize energy into Low / Medium / High using tertiles\\n\",\n",
    "    \"energy_quantiles = pd.qcut(nutrient_df['energy'], q=3, labels=['Low', 'Medium', 'High'], duplicates='drop')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"nutrient_df['energy_group'] = energy_quantiles\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Step 2: Categorize fat into Low / Medium / High using tertiles\\n\",\n",
    "    \"fat_quantiles = pd.qcut(nutrient_df['fat'], q=3, labels=['Low', 'Medium', 'High'], duplicates='drop')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"nutrient_df['fat_group'] = fat_quantiles\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('=== Nutrient Data with Energy and Fat Groups ===')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(nutrient_df[['Food_Item', 'energy', 'energy_group', 'fat', 'fat_group']])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('\\\\n=== Group Distribution ===')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('Energy Groups:')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(nutrient_df['energy_group'].value_counts().sort_index())\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('\\\\nFat Groups:')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(nutrient_df['fat_group'].value_counts().sort_index())\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Step-by-step calculation of nominal similarity using simple matching\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"def nominal_similarity(row1, row2, df):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Compute simple matching similarity based on nominal attribute matches.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Parameters:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    row1, row2: row indices in the DataFrame\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    df: DataFrame with energy_group and fat_group columns\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Returns:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Dictionary with calculation details\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Get the groups for both items\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    item1 = df.iloc[row1]['Food_Item']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    item2 = df.iloc[row2]['Food_Item']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    energy1 = df.iloc[row1]['energy_group']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    energy2 = df.iloc[row2]['energy_group']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    fat1 = df.iloc[row1]['fat_group']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    fat2 = df.iloc[row2]['fat_group']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Check matches\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    energy_match = 1 if energy1 == energy2 else 0\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    fat_match = 1 if fat1 == fat2 else 0\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Simple matching coefficient\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    total_attributes = 2\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    matches = energy_match + fat_match\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    similarity = matches / total_attributes\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return {\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'item1': item1,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'item2': item2,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'energy1': energy1,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'energy2': energy2,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'fat1': fat1,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'fat2': fat2,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'energy_match': energy_match,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'fat_match': fat_match,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'total_matches': matches,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'similarity': similarity\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    }\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Example: Compare first three food items (rows 0, 1, 2)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('=== Nominal Similarity Calculation - Step by Step ===\\\\n')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Pair 1: BEEF BRAISED vs HAMBURGER\\n\",\n",
    "    \"result1 = nominal_similarity(0, 1, nutrient_df)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('--- Pair 1: BEEF BRAISED vs HAMBURGER ---')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Energy Groups: {result1['energy1']} vs {result1['energy2']} → Match: {result1['energy_match']}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Fat Groups: {result1['fat1']} vs {result1['fat2']} → Match: {result1['fat_match']}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Total Matches: {result1['total_matches']} / 2\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Similarity: {result1['similarity']:.2f}\\\\n\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Pair 2: BEEF BRAISED vs BEEF ROAST\\n\",\n",
    "    \"result2 = nominal_similarity(0, 2, nutrient_df)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('--- Pair 2: BEEF BRAISED vs BEEF ROAST ---')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Energy Groups: {result2['energy1']} vs {result2['energy2']} → Match: {result2['energy_match']}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Fat Groups: {result2['fat1']} vs {result2['fat2']} → Match: {result2['fat_match']}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Total Matches: {result2['total_matches']} / 2\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Similarity: {result2['similarity']:.2f}\\\\n\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Pair 3: HAMBURGER vs CHICKEN BROILED\\n\",\n",
    "    \"result3 = nominal_similarity(1, 5, nutrient_df)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('--- Pair 3: HAMBURGER vs CHICKEN BROILED ---')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Energy Groups: {result3['energy1']} vs {result3['energy2']} → Match: {result3['energy_match']}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Fat Groups: {result3['fat1']} vs {result3['fat2']} → Match: {result3['fat_match']}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Total Matches: {result3['total_matches']} / 2\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Similarity: {result3['similarity']:.2f}\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Task 26 – Binary Attributes: Jaccard Similarity and SMC\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Task 26: Create binary attributes and compute Jaccard + SMC\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Step 1: Calculate median values for protein and iron\\n\",\n",
    "    \"median_protein = nutrient_df['protein'].median()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"median_iron = nutrient_df['iron'].median()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'=== Median Values ===')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'Median Protein: {median_protein:.2f}')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f'Median Iron: {median_iron:.2f}')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Step 2: Create binary attributes\\n\",\n",
    "    \"nutrient_df['high_protein'] = (nutrient_df['protein'] > median_protein).astype(int)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"nutrient_df['high_iron'] = (nutrient_df['iron'] > median_iron).astype(int)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('\\\\n=== Binary Attributes Created ===')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(nutrient_df[['Food_Item', 'protein', 'high_protein', 'iron', 'high_iron']])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('\\\\n=== Binary Attribute Distribution ===')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('High Protein:')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(nutrient_df['high_protein'].value_counts())\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('\\\\nHigh Iron:')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(nutrient_df['high_iron'].value_counts())\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Compute Jaccard Similarity and Simple Matching Coefficient (SMC)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"def jaccard_similarity(a, b):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Compute Jaccard similarity between two binary vectors.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Jaccard = M11 / (M01 + M10 + M11)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Ignores mutual absence (M00)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    M11 = np.sum((a == 1) & (b == 1))  # Both 1\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    M01 = np.sum((a == 0) & (b == 1))  # a=0, b=1\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    M10 = np.sum((a == 1) & (b == 0))  # a=1, b=0\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    denominator = M01 + M10 + M11\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if denominator == 0:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        return 0\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return M11 / denominator\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"def smc(a, b):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Compute Simple Matching Coefficient between two binary vectors.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    SMC = (M11 + M00) / (M00 + M01 + M10 + M11)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Considers both mutual presence and mutual absence\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    M11 = np.sum((a == 1) & (b == 1))  # Both 1\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    M00 = np.sum((a == 0) & (b == 0))  # Both 0\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    M01 = np.sum((a == 0) & (b == 1))  # a=0, b=1\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    M10 = np.sum((a == 1) & (b == 0))  # a=1, b=0\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    total = M00 + M01 + M10 + M11\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if total == 0:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        return 0\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return (M11 + M00) / total\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Select three pairs of food items\\n\",\n",
    "    \"pair_indices = [(0, 1), (0, 5), (5, 24)]  # Different combinations\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('=== Jaccard Similarity and SMC Calculation ===\\\\n')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"binary_results = []\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for idx1, idx2 in pair_indices:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    item1 = nutrient_df.iloc[idx1]['Food_Item']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    item2 = nutrient_df.iloc[idx2]['Food_Item']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Get binary vectors\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    vec1 = nutrient_df.iloc[idx1][['high_protein', 'high_iron']].values\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    vec2 = nutrient_df.iloc[idx2][['high_protein', 'high_iron']].values\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Compute similarities\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    jaccard = jaccard_similarity(vec1, vec2)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    smc_val = smc(vec1, vec2)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Calculate matching details\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    M11 = np.sum((vec1 == 1) & (vec2 == 1))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    M00 = np.sum((vec1 == 0) & (vec2 == 0))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    M01 = np.sum((vec1 == 0) & (vec2 == 1))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    M10 = np.sum((vec1 == 1) & (vec2 == 0))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    binary_results.append({\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'pair': f'{item1} vs {item2}',\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'vec1': vec1,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'vec2': vec2,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'M11': M11,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'M00': M00,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'M01': M01,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'M10': M10,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'jaccard': jaccard,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'smc': smc_val\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    })\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f'Pair: {item1} vs {item2}')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f'  Binary vectors: {vec1} vs {vec2}')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f'  M11 (both 1): {M11}, M00 (both 0): {M00}, M01: {M01}, M10: {M10}')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f'  Jaccard Similarity: {jaccard:.4f}')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f'  SMC: {smc_val:.4f}')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Create summary table\\n\",\n",
    "    \"summary_df = pd.DataFrame([\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    {\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'Pair': r['pair'],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'M11': r['M11'],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'M00': r['M00'],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'M01': r['M01'],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'M10': r['M10'],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'Jaccard': round(r['jaccard'], 4),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        'SMC': round(r['smc'], 4)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    }\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for r in binary_results\\n\",\n",
    "    \"])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print('=== Summary Table ===')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(summary_df)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Discussion: Jaccard vs. Simple Matching Coefficient (SMC)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"**Key Differences Between Jaccard and SMC:**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. **Treatment of Mutual Absence (M00):**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   - **Jaccard Similarity:** Ignores M00 (cases where both attributes are 0). Formula: $J = \\\\frac{M_{11}}{M_{01} + M_{10} + M_{11}}$\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   - **SMC:** Includes M00 in the calculation. Formula: $SMC = \\\\frac{M_{11} + M_{00}}{M_{00} + M_{01} + M_{10} + M_{11}}$\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. **Context of Asymmetric Binary Attributes:**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   - In our nutrient dataset, `high_protein` and `high_iron` are **asymmetric binary attributes** — having a value of 1 (high) is more informative than having a value of 0 (not high)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   - The presence of a trait (high protein/iron) is more significant than its absence\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"3. **When to Use Each:**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   - **Jaccard** is preferred for asymmetric binary attributes because it focuses on shared presences (M11) rather than shared absences (M00). Two items being \\\"both not high\\\" in protein doesn't indicate true similarity.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   - **SMC** is suitable for symmetric binary attributes where both presence and absence carry equal weight.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"4. **Observed Values:**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   - When both items share the same binary values (e.g., both high protein AND high iron), Jaccard = SMC = 1.0\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   - When items differ, Jaccard tends to be **lower** than SMC because it excludes M00 from the denominator\\n\",\n",
    "    \"   - Jaccard provides a **more conservative** similarity estimate for asymmetric attributes\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Conclusion:** For the nutrient data's binary attributes (high_protein, high_iron), **Jaccard similarity is more appropriate** because it emphasizes shared positive traits rather than shared negatives, which aligns with how we intuitively compare nutritional profiles.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
